      "slides": [
        {
          "title": "New maker for the maglia rosa",
          "text": "MAAP has signed a multi-year partnership with RCS to provide apparel across its races, including the men's and women's Giro d'Italia leaders' jerseys."
        },
        {
          "title": "Which races are covered",
          "text": "The deal also covers Tirreno-Adriatico and the Giro Next Gen. Jerseys will also be made for one-day races like Milan-San Remo, Strade Bianche and Il Lombardia, but not worn in the race or awarded to winners."
        },
        {
          "title": "A different look is expected",
          "text": "Cyclingnews understands the new pink jersey will be a significant departure from the Castelli design. It is not due to be revealed until sometime in the New Year."
        },
        {
          "title": "MAAP's rapid rise",
          "text": "Founded in Melbourne in 2014, MAAP entered the European pro peloton in 2024 with Lifeplus-Wahoo and now makes the Jayco-AlUla and Liv-AlUla Jayco kits."
        }
